WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634
-Welcome back. Good to see you.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.170
-I'm always so happy to have you
here. You did a very nice thing.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
In your hometown of
Traverse City, Michigan,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.541 line:92%
you own a couple movie theaters.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Beautiful --
-Some old theaters.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.379 line:92%
I restored them as a nonprofit

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
and donated them
to the community, yeah.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.049 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-During the shutdown,

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:19.586
you were letting federal workers
come for free.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Yeah.
And their families.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.823 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
Free popcorn, free pop.
-Free popcorn and free pop.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's great.
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait. You guys
call popcorn pop?

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. Soda is pop.
-All right. Good.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Popcorn is popcorn.
-Okay. Good.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:36.069
I was worried there was, like,
some weird Traverse City slang.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:36.870 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-No, no, no. We are --

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
The closer you get to Canada,
words do change.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And people get nicer.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:43.376
-They do. The closer you get
to Canada, they get nicer.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.079
I want to thank you. You gave us
some very nice promotion.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.580 size:81% position:41%
You wore a "Late Night
with Seth Meyers" hat

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "All In with Chris Hayes."
-Oh, that's right.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
I promised I'd wear
a Chris Hayes hat tonight.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
-Oh, I'm so -- He's in bed.

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:57.357
-Oh, yeah. He won't be...
You know what we'll do?

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll just digitally
put in there.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll get our digital-effects
team to make it a...

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:04.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, there you go.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we have so much
to talk about.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were obviously mentioning
Howard Schultz

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:09.836 size:84% position:42% line:92%
at the top of the show.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you feel about --
-The self-made Howard Schultz.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, now, explain this.
-Yes, yes.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You take issue with
"self-made."

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.511 line:92%
-Well, in the same sentence,

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
he goes,
"I'm a self-made billionaire.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
I grew up in the projects
in Brooklyn."

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.251 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Right away, by admitting

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you had subsidized
public housing

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
paid for by the tax dollars
of the American people,

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.992 size:78% position:39% line:92%
you aren't self-made.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:37.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got a hand up from us,
like we want to do.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
We want to help
our fellow Americans.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a form of socialism,
public housing.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.738 size:75% position:38%
And yet he's saying,
"I'm all self-made."

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.340 line:92%
He went to a public university.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
He went to Northern Michigan
University, actually.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:53.179
And, you know, again,
financed by taxpayers' dollars.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.281 line:92%
And, then, he sells coffee,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.852
which is essentially water,
using city water systems.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Municipal water systems.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Which, you know...

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.491 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's, like,
a huge infrastructure

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know,
if you have a business,

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
you might have to
have FedEx or trucks

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.499 line:92%
deliver things to your store.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:16.769
He has the people in New York
and all these other cities

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.272 size:75% position:38%
delivering the water
underground to him.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, then, you know
what your water bill is.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody -- It's --
Of all the utility bills,

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:26.813
it's your least expensive bill,
right?

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I did the calculation
earlier today.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.218 line:92%
It's like 100th of a penny

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:37.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
to fill up a grande cup
at Starbucks.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:40.593 line:92%
100th of a penny for that water.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:43.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to say,
"Oh, I got to be a..."

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.031 line:92%
You got to be a billionaire

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we're paying
for the water!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.501 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
If he was just giving people
a cup of coffee grounds,

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.205 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that would be one thing.

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The beans are probably
another penny.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
The coffee bean.
-You have a way --

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have an idea
to pressure him not to run.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:00.947 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What's your idea?

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, my idea, first of all,
is none of us

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:06.252
should go to Starbucks until
he announces he's not running.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:06.786 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha. Okay.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:10.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then you can go back
and buy a $5 cup of coffee.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
But in the meantime,
I was thinking

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
that those of us who would
support such a boycott,

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.796
we could set up, like, a little
table in front of Starbucks,

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a lemonade stand,
and provide coffee,

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.968
because people need their
coffee, I understand that.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.103 size:78% position:39%
So, we'll have coffee
there at Starbucks

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:27.974
but in front of Starbucks
with city-owned water.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There you go.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.311 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So...

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:34.480
-Again, we're starting to see --
You know, it's still early days.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's sort of a trickle
of candidates

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.751 size:88% position:44%
that I think is going to
only increase in size.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.852 line:92%
We're starting to see platforms.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you were running,
what would be your platforms?

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:44.257
What would be the things
that Michael Moore would promise

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.291 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to the American people?

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.127
-Well, I have a number of things
I would do.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:51.864
First of all, I love the idea
of just outlawing billionaires.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.133 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It really is immoral.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:58.071
I mean, I understand, you know,
you can make $900 million

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.740
and get through the year
with that as your income.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:04.344
But the idea of a billionaire --
I was thinking about --

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.745 line:92%
We were talking backstage here.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're on 50th Street
and Sixth Avenue

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.782 size:81% position:41% line:92%
here in New York City.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:13.553
Two nights ago, a young mother,
22 years old,

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the subway stop
one block over

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
on Seventh avenue
and 50th Street,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:21.494
trying to take her baby
down the stairs in the stroller,

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:24.964 line:92%
and she falls and she dies.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:25.832 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The mother dies.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
The baby lived,
but the mother died.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:32.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like -- This is the
richest country on the planet,

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:33.106 line:92%
and we're in the richest city,

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.976
and we have a subway system
that is over 100 years old

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
and feels like
it's 200 years old.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:42.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the fact
that we can't even provide

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
what you have in other cities
in this country,

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.419 line:92%
but also throughout the world --

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:49.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
mass transit,
modern mass transit --

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:54.127
and she has to die struggling to
take a stroller down the stairs.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:57.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nine blocks from us
right here --

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:02.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
go the other direction,
on 59th and Sixth Avenue --

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
a man just bought
the most expensive

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:08.374 line:92%
home, dwelling, in America.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
He spent $238 million
on his penthouse.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-On Central Park South.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:19.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
How could we just
nine blocks away have that

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:24.123
and allow this woman to die
because of an infrastructure

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:26.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has crumbled
and doesn't work?

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:29.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
If I were president,
I would fix that immediately.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:34.701
I would not allow this kind
of disparity to continue.

